From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:05:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac: don't log an error per transfer
 without apb_regs

Platforms like the StarFive JH7110 have no APB register block for the
AXI DMA controller. dw_axi_dma_set_hw_channel() then logs an error for
every transfer (e.g. continuously while playing audio), flooding the
console. Use dev_dbg(), as dw_axi_dma_set_byte_halfword() already does.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
index 7520c78f55..d8b6bc4e8d 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
@@ -576,7 +576,7 @@ static void dw_axi_dma_set_hw_channel(struct axi_dma_chan *chan, bool set)
 	unsigned long reg_value, val;
 
 	if (!chip->apb_regs) {
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "apb_regs not initialized\n");
+		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "apb_regs not initialized\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
